# Build context exclusions for `docker build -f apps/<app>/Dockerfile .`
#
# Both images are built from the REPOSITORY ROOT, not from the app directory:
# this is a pnpm workspace and `packages/schemas` is a real dependency of both
# apps, so the context has to contain the whole workspace. Everything below is
# what must NOT travel with it.

# ---- never, under any circumstance ----
# Secrets. The images read their configuration from the environment at run
# time (compose.prod.yaml + the operator's .env.production); a .env baked into
# a layer is a secret published to everyone who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
apps/*/.env
apps/*/.env.*
packages/*/.env

# ---- host build output; the image builds its own ----
# Copying these in is not just waste: a Windows-built node_modules carries
# win32 native binaries (argon2, sharp, @img/sharp-win32-x64) that would
# shadow the linux ones the image installs.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- test, audit and asset artefacts ----
test-results
playwright-report
screenshots
coverage
e2e
docs/shots
tmp

# ---- reference-only prototype (CLAUDE.md §13) ----
# Not part of the pnpm workspace and never imported by apps/* or packages/*.
legacy

# ---- 113 MB of render masters that feed scripts/optimize-landing.mjs ----
# Only its committed output under apps/web/public/landing/ ships.
landing-src

# ---- repo prose; nothing in either build reads it ----
*.md
!apps/**/*.md
docs

# ---- local tooling and VCS ----
.git
.github
.husky
.claude
.vscode
.idea
playwright.config.ts
compose.yaml
compose.prod.yaml
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
